Usage: cape submission report [--dry-run] [--keep-existing] <benchmark>
       cape submission report [--dry-run] [--keep-existing] --all

Generate interactive HTML performance reports comparing submission performance.

Arguments:
  <benchmark>    Name of the benchmark to generate report for
  --all          Generate reports for all benchmarks with submissions

Options:
  --dry-run       Show actions without writing files
  --keep-existing Do not delete the existing report/ directory before generating

The report includes:
- Main index page (report/index.html) listing all benchmarks
- Individual benchmark report pages (report/benchmarks/<benchmark>.html)
- Per-submission evaluation breakdown pages
  (report/benchmarks/<benchmark>/<submission_dir>.html), linked from each
  submission row on the benchmark page
- Selectable ranking criterion, shared by scenario winners and comparison charts
- Fee, CPU and memory with sum, mean, median, minimum and maximum aggregations
- Script/AST size, transaction capacity and budget percentages

The default ranking is the sum of execution costs of positive measured cases,
plus the reference-script fee once. Failure-path checks and pending cases are
excluded. The selected criterion and aggregation are preserved in the URL.

Each submission is labeled as: {language}_{version}_{user}

Output:
  report/index.html                           # Main index with all benchmarks
  report/benchmarks/<benchmark>.html          # Individual benchmark reports
  report/benchmarks/<benchmark>/<dir>.html    # Per-submission evaluation breakdowns
  report/benchmarks/<benchmark>.json         # Comparison data

Examples:
  cape submission report fibonacci           # Report for fibonacci benchmark
  cape submission report --all               # Reports for all benchmarks

Requirements:
  - gomplate and jq must be installed
  - Submissions must have metrics.json files (use 'cape submission measure')
